# Cross-frame Bounds propagation (error-model.md §11, Increment 2.1d): an
# out-of-bounds index INSIDE a callee (`getx`) propagates to a
# `catch Fault.Bounds` in its DIRECT caller (`main`), without unwind — the
# callee's `xs[i]` routes the OOB (NULL from gorget_array_safe_get) into the
# Bounds fault-return block, writing the Bounds tag into a hidden trailing slot;
# the caller reads the tag and dispatches to the handler. Expected stdout: 999.
int getx(Vector[int] xs, int i): xs[i]    # may OOB; NO local catch

void main():
    Vector[int] xs = [10, 20, 30]
    int r = getx(xs, 99) catch Fault.Bounds: 999
    print(f"{r}")
